    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-113893",
      "knowledge_point_id": "8bd8c6d8-0b11-5735-88a1-9b12e6315401",
      "knowledge_point": "Integrating an Exponential Function With a General Base",
      "problem": "Calculate $\\int {(\\frac{1}{8})}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "To compute the integral of a general exponential function, we just need to divide by the natural logarithm of the base of the exponential function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {(\\frac{1}{8})}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{(\\frac{1}{8})}^{x}}{ln⁡(\\frac{1}{8})}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the laws of logarithms, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ln⁡(\\frac{1}{8}) & =ln⁡1-ln⁡8 \\\\  & =0-ln⁡8 \\\\  & =-ln⁡8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can simplify our final answer as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{(\\frac{1}{8})}^{x}}{ln⁡(\\frac{1}{8})}+C=-\\frac{{(\\frac{1}{8})}^{x}}{ln⁡8}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "-\\frac{ln⁡x}{{8}^{x}}+C"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{(\\frac{1}{8})}^{x}ln⁡8+C"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{ln⁡x}{ln⁡8}+C"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "-\\frac{{(\\frac{1}{8})}^{x}}{ln⁡8}+C"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{{8}^{x}}{ln⁡8}+C"
            }
          ],
          "correct_value": "-\\frac{{(\\frac{1}{8})}^{x}}{ln⁡8}+C"
        }
      ],
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "provenance": {
        "activity_question": "question-113893",
        "kp_title": "Integrating an Exponential Function With a General Base",
        "kp_href": null
      }
